WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.842
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.112 --> 00:09.114
[theme music playing]

3
00:30.135 --> 00:31.595
[banging on door]

4
00:32.972 --> 00:35.850
[Woo-jin's father] Open up! I said open the door!

5
00:35.933 --> 00:37.059
[banging on door]

6
00:37.643 --> 00:40.646
Gah! Come on! Open it! Your dad's here, you little brat!

7
00:41.689 --> 00:44.567
-Why, you little punk. [grunts] -[banging on door]

8
00:48.654 --> 00:50.656
[grunting]

9
01:03.419 --> 01:04.795
[metal clattering on floor]

10
01:04.879 --> 01:06.797
You goddamn little brat.

11
01:06.881 --> 01:08.215
You lock the damn door on me?

12
01:08.299 --> 01:09.967
I'm sorry.

13
01:10.050 --> 01:11.552
Yeah. Sure, it's fine.

14
01:14.179 --> 01:17.099
-Hey, you little brat. -I'm sorry.

15
01:17.182 --> 01:18.434
What'd you say?

16
01:18.517 --> 01:19.727
I was wrong.

17
01:19.810 --> 01:21.437
You were wrong? Huh?

18
01:21.520 --> 01:24.315
-Do you even know what you did wrong? Huh? -Yes.

19
01:24.899 --> 01:26.525
Your bitch of a mother's run off.

20
01:26.609 --> 01:28.319
God knows where or what she's doing right now.

21
01:28.402 --> 01:30.863
And you're here sleeping without a damn care in the world.

22
01:31.530 --> 01:32.698
I'm sorry.

23
01:32.781 --> 01:35.117
Look at you, all fat and well-fed.

24
01:35.200 --> 01:38.370
Must be nice, living the good life, you little brat.

25
01:38.454 --> 01:39.747
[groaning]

26
01:41.832 --> 01:42.833
Damn it.

27
01:43.334 --> 01:45.502
[coughing]

28
01:51.842 --> 01:55.095
[coughing, gasping]

29
02:12.363 --> 02:15.282
-[grunts] Damn. You little rat. -[doorknob rattling]

30
02:15.950 --> 02:17.868
Hey! I'm asking nicely. Open up.

31
02:17.952 --> 02:19.536
Open up, you bastard!

32
02:19.620 --> 02:22.289
[coughing]

33
02:22.373 --> 02:23.666
Open up, now!

34
02:25.459 --> 02:26.877
Hey, Cha Woo-jin!

35
02:26.961 --> 02:29.505
[coughing continues]

36
02:29.588 --> 02:32.758
Open the damn door, you bastard!

37
02:32.841 --> 02:34.843
-Open it! You little bastard! -[screams]

38
02:34.927 --> 02:37.763
-Open up right now. [coughing] -[screaming]

39
02:37.846 --> 02:39.431
Open the door!

40
02:39.515 --> 02:41.809
I said open it, you bastard!

41
02:41.892 --> 02:44.395
[coughing]

42
02:48.148 --> 02:49.566
[gasps]

43
02:56.281 --> 02:58.158
-[breathing rapidly] -Open it.

44
02:59.034 --> 03:00.035
Open it.

45
03:01.161 --> 03:02.162
I said open…

46
03:02.997 --> 03:04.456
Open…

47
03:04.540 --> 03:06.041
You damn brat…

48
03:06.125 --> 03:08.836
Open the door… [grunting, gasping]

49
03:10.587 --> 03:13.340
[cries out, panting]

50
03:20.723 --> 03:22.599
[food sizzling]

51
03:25.102 --> 03:26.103
[gasps]

52
03:28.439 --> 03:29.606
[stove top beeps]

53
03:57.551 --> 03:59.720
[Hae-seon] You're okay, Chris. Hang in there.

54
04:07.519 --> 04:08.604
Goodness.

55
04:10.105 --> 04:11.356
Look at all this sweat.

56
04:11.440 --> 04:12.524
Seriously.

57
04:12.608 --> 04:15.444
Just stay seated. We already called an ambulance for you.

58
04:15.527 --> 04:17.821
I'm fine. It's… just anemia.

59
04:18.405 --> 04:19.615
The adrenaline just wore off.

60
04:19.698 --> 04:21.325
It didn't seem like simple anemia.

61
04:21.408 --> 04:25.162
Come on. Let's get you to a hospital and have you checked out.

62
04:31.627 --> 04:32.795
I really am fine.

63
04:42.054 --> 04:45.015
I'm sorry for the trouble, Chairwoman.

64
05:05.452 --> 05:06.620
[chiming, beeping]

65
05:08.372 --> 05:10.874
I had a very strange dream the other night.

66
05:10.958 --> 05:13.961
It was about a peacock, I think. Or was it a pheasant?

67
05:14.044 --> 05:16.046
Come on. Give me something.

68
05:23.220 --> 05:24.972
[fanfare plays on game]

69
05:27.057 --> 05:31.145
[shouts, laughing]

70
05:33.188 --> 05:35.065
It was a peacock.

71
05:35.149 --> 05:38.277
[laughing]

72
05:38.360 --> 05:40.904
-[shouts, laughing] -[phone chimes]

73
05:50.122 --> 05:51.290
[buzzing]

74
05:53.625 --> 05:54.835
[treadmill beeps]

75
05:59.339 --> 06:00.674
THE TABLE ASSISTANT DIRECTOR

76
06:00.757 --> 06:03.844
"This round's cooking challenge will take place away from the studio."

77
06:04.469 --> 06:08.307
"We'll be traveling some distance to a place with clean water and fresh air, so…"

78
06:08.390 --> 06:09.391
[Ok-seon] "Chefs, please,

79
06:09.474 --> 06:11.810
pack enough clothes and essentials for a five-day trip…"

80
06:11.894 --> 06:15.355
"And meet at the rear entrance of the broadcasting station…"

81
06:16.064 --> 06:17.983
[Ja-ryong] "Next Wednesday at 9:00 a.m."

82
06:19.401 --> 06:20.402
Five days?

83
06:20.485 --> 06:22.613
What, are we gonna close the restaurant for five days?

84
06:22.696 --> 06:24.573
They're not compensating us.

85
06:24.656 --> 06:28.327
Exactly. What kind of challenge takes five days?

86
06:28.410 --> 06:30.162
[scoffs] Isn't this a bit much?

87
06:30.245 --> 06:33.081
The other teams won't be happy about this either.

88
06:42.216 --> 06:43.926
-Listen, Chef Oh. -Yes, Chef.

89
06:44.009 --> 06:47.346
You'll be in charge of Exception for those five days.

90
06:47.429 --> 06:48.555
Sorry?

91
06:49.681 --> 06:51.308
-Michael. -Yes, Chef.

92
06:51.391 --> 06:53.977
-Pick a fill-in from the garde-manger. -What?

93
06:55.062 --> 06:56.188
Right. Understood, Chef.

94
07:04.154 --> 07:05.697
THE TABLE ASSISTANT DIRECTOR

95
07:05.781 --> 07:07.741
[Geon-woo] Business is already slow enough,

96
07:07.824 --> 07:10.661
and now they want us to close the restaurant for five days.

97
07:12.537 --> 07:13.580
What are you going to do?

98
07:15.249 --> 07:18.043
I don't know. Five whole days…

99
07:19.127 --> 07:20.545
What should we do?

100
07:29.513 --> 07:30.514
Chris.

101
07:34.559 --> 07:36.603
-Chris. -Huh?

102
07:38.981 --> 07:40.190
Oh.

103
07:41.733 --> 07:45.362
[sighs] Sorry. I'm going upstairs to rest for a bit.

104
07:55.122 --> 07:56.373
[sighs]

105
07:57.124 --> 08:00.252
He's had no energy at all since we got back from filming yesterday.

106
08:01.295 --> 08:02.462
What's going on?

107
08:13.390 --> 08:15.267
[gentle music playing]

108
08:18.770 --> 08:20.564
[grunts]

109
08:23.567 --> 08:24.609
[sighs]

110
08:34.119 --> 08:36.621
Han, wake up. Han.

111
08:37.664 --> 08:40.792
Uh, why, Dad? I'm sleepy.

112
08:40.876 --> 08:43.003
We have to pack and leave. There's no time.

113
08:43.086 --> 08:46.256
Huh? Why? Are we moving again?

114
08:46.840 --> 08:49.718
They found out where we are now. They're coming after us.

115
08:51.219 --> 08:52.596
Get dressed. Quickly.

116
08:54.806 --> 08:56.058
[knocking on door]

117
08:58.060 --> 08:59.061
Who's that?

118
09:00.395 --> 09:01.396
[knocking harder]

119
09:02.939 --> 09:04.316
Uh, Dad…

120
09:06.818 --> 09:08.070
[knocking continues]

121
09:09.279 --> 09:10.364
[younger Hae-seon] Han.

122
09:10.447 --> 09:11.448
Kang Han!

123
09:12.407 --> 09:14.785
Han, wake up, come on. Huh?

124
09:15.452 --> 09:16.912
[younger Hae-seon] Come on, wake up.

125
09:16.995 --> 09:18.330
Kang Han!

126
09:18.413 --> 09:19.748
Chris, please, wake up.

127
09:19.831 --> 09:22.584
-[younger Hae-seon] Han. Kang Han. -[Hae-seon] Chris. Chris, wake up!

128
09:22.667 --> 09:24.336
-Kang Han! -Chris!

129
09:24.419 --> 09:25.670
-Han. -Chris.

130
09:25.754 --> 09:27.464
-Han! -Chris, wake up.

131
09:27.547 --> 09:30.175
Can you hear me? Chris!

132
09:30.842 --> 09:32.177
Chris, wake up, come on!

133
09:32.969 --> 09:34.137
Chris!

134
09:40.685 --> 09:42.729
You'll die too if you stay here.

135
09:42.813 --> 09:44.106
-Do as I say. -[teenage Han] No, Dad!

136
09:44.189 --> 09:45.732
Listen to me now.

137
09:46.608 --> 09:47.692
Just go!

138
09:47.776 --> 09:49.444
Pyeongyeon Group killed my father.

139
09:49.528 --> 09:51.363
Pyeongyeon Group was responsible for my father's death.

140
09:51.446 --> 09:54.533
They fabricated a bunch of lies and drove him to take his own life.

141
09:54.616 --> 09:56.201
Pyeongyeon killed Dad.

142
09:56.284 --> 09:58.370
I said Pyeongyeon killed Dad!

143
09:59.287 --> 10:00.789
[screaming]

144
10:00.872 --> 10:01.873
[teenage Han] Dad!

145
10:02.749 --> 10:06.169
[gasping]

146
10:08.296 --> 10:10.799
[breathing rapidly]

147
10:13.552 --> 10:14.553
Chris.

148
10:18.014 --> 10:19.266
Song.

149
10:40.704 --> 10:42.747
Sorry for just coming in like this.

150
10:43.790 --> 10:47.252
But you looked really unwell. And also, I thought I heard something.

151
10:58.638 --> 10:59.806
Chris.

152
11:00.724 --> 11:03.101
Are you really okay?

153
11:03.685 --> 11:07.230
You collapsed yesterday, too, and you look really exhausted.

154
11:08.148 --> 11:10.484
Let's go to the hospital right now, so they can…

155
11:10.567 --> 11:11.568
Song.

156
11:12.944 --> 11:13.987
I'm okay.

157
11:16.948 --> 11:19.868
This happens sometimes when I stay cooped up in the kitchen

158
11:20.785 --> 11:22.078
under too much stress.

159
11:23.955 --> 11:25.540
You don't have to worry.

160
11:25.624 --> 11:27.334
It's nothing serious. I swear.

161
11:29.169 --> 11:30.545
I just need some rest.

162
11:30.629 --> 11:31.630
That's all.

163
11:33.089 --> 11:33.924
Chris.

164
11:34.591 --> 11:36.885
Come on, let me take you to the hospital.

165
11:38.053 --> 11:39.721
You seem to have a fever too.

166
11:40.555 --> 11:41.640
Let's go to the hospital.

167
11:41.723 --> 11:43.934
They can run some tests and see if it's anything serious.

168
11:44.017 --> 11:45.810
I already told you that I'm fine.

169
11:50.232 --> 11:51.942
Come on, let's go.

170
11:52.025 --> 11:53.652
I'm so worried about you, Chris.

171
11:53.735 --> 11:55.111
Song, please!

172
12:18.218 --> 12:19.386
I'm sorry.

173
12:21.346 --> 12:23.014
I'm sorry I worried you.

174
12:25.183 --> 12:26.226
But I'm…

175
12:27.310 --> 12:28.395
I'm really okay.

176
12:38.530 --> 12:39.698
Hey.

177
12:40.282 --> 12:42.117
You can believe me.

178
12:42.200 --> 12:43.868
I really am okay.

179
12:47.706 --> 12:48.915
We should practice.

180
12:49.541 --> 12:52.002
Go downstairs and start prepping. I'll be right there.

181
12:59.968 --> 13:01.886
ELEMENTARY SCHOOL, COLLEGE GRADUATION, CHEF DAYS…

182
13:03.305 --> 13:05.724
This is his biological father.

183
13:06.224 --> 13:08.852
And this white man is his adoptive father.

184
13:08.935 --> 13:10.645
His adoptive father owned the restaurant

185
13:10.729 --> 13:13.315
where his biological father, Kang San, worked.

186
13:13.398 --> 13:14.858
They must've been very close.

187
13:14.941 --> 13:17.027
After San died, he adopted his son.

188
13:17.110 --> 13:19.321
His name was Kang Han at that time.

189
13:19.988 --> 13:22.407
Until he was adopted, he never attended school.

190
13:22.490 --> 13:23.742
He was home-schooled.

191
13:23.825 --> 13:26.745
Even that was informal schooling through a Korean church,

192
13:26.828 --> 13:29.080
so there's not even a paper trail left.

193
13:29.164 --> 13:30.248
What a shame.

194
13:30.790 --> 13:33.960
According to a tutor we finally managed to track down,

195
13:34.753 --> 13:35.754
he was called…

196
13:36.546 --> 13:38.340
"Honey" by his folks at home.

197
13:39.132 --> 13:42.636
Well, his name is "Han." Americanize it from… "Han-i."

198
13:42.719 --> 13:43.720
"Han-i."

199
13:44.304 --> 13:45.305
"Heonie."

200
13:46.056 --> 13:48.183
"Honey." So I guess it stuck.

201
13:48.266 --> 13:50.101
"Honey"?

202
13:50.185 --> 13:53.521
-[scoffs] Sounds like a girl's name. -[chuckles]

203
13:53.605 --> 13:55.148
Hang on.

204
13:55.231 --> 13:59.152
When I lived in the States, the family across the street had a dog.

205
13:59.235 --> 14:01.071
Named Honey too. Honey.

206
14:01.154 --> 14:05.700
The dad, the mom and the kids, they were always going, "Honey, Honey, Honey."

207
14:05.784 --> 14:06.785
All day long!

208
14:07.452 --> 14:11.373
[laughing] That dog was ugly as heck.

209
14:11.956 --> 14:14.793
Nothing like the cute name the family gave him.

210
14:16.670 --> 14:18.672
Is that why they named it that?

211
14:18.755 --> 14:20.298
So at least it'd have a cute name?

212
14:20.382 --> 14:22.509
Well… Well, I guess so.

213
14:24.678 --> 14:27.347
He really moved around a lot. Look at this.

214
14:27.430 --> 14:30.308
No wonder it was so hard to find any papers on him.

215
14:31.101 --> 14:33.937
Man, those tenacious bastards.

216
14:44.823 --> 14:48.034
I thought he had died back then.

217
14:48.118 --> 14:49.703
He's grown up quite well.

218
14:50.745 --> 14:52.080
[chuckles]

219
14:52.163 --> 14:53.164
Interesting.

220
14:54.541 --> 14:57.127
To meet again like this. [chuckling]

221
14:58.002 --> 15:00.213
Live long enough, you'll see everything.

222
15:00.296 --> 15:03.717
[laughing]

223
15:11.725 --> 15:13.143
Hang on.

224
15:13.226 --> 15:15.603
Go back to where they make eye contact.

225
15:20.525 --> 15:21.484
Pause there.

226
15:23.987 --> 15:25.280
Play.

227
15:28.658 --> 15:30.827
Go back to where Chris starts talking to him.

228
15:30.910 --> 15:32.078
Play it in slo-mo.

229
15:34.497 --> 15:36.249
[mysterious music playing]

230
15:41.880 --> 15:43.298
What do you think he's saying?

231
15:45.175 --> 15:47.761
Either way, it doesn't look like a friendly conversation, does it?

232
15:47.844 --> 15:49.220
-No. -No.

233
15:49.971 --> 15:51.598
Judging by their expressions,

234
15:51.681 --> 15:53.683
it does look like they're having a tense exchange.

235
15:53.767 --> 15:54.768
Mmm.

236
15:56.060 --> 15:57.312
[producer] It's strange though.

237
15:57.395 --> 15:58.938
From the exchange,

238
15:59.022 --> 16:01.900
I get the sense they've known each other for a very long time.

239
16:01.983 --> 16:03.943
Yeah. I think you're right.

240
16:04.027 --> 16:07.363
It's almost like picking up right where they left off some day before.

241
16:34.182 --> 16:35.016
SEA SALT

242
16:35.099 --> 16:36.518
SEA SALT

243
16:39.312 --> 16:41.314
70 GRAMS, 0.90%

244
17:11.302 --> 17:13.179
[chattering]

245
17:18.893 --> 17:21.187
[gentle music playing]

246
17:24.399 --> 17:25.733
[bell ringing]

247
17:42.458 --> 17:44.002
[mechanical whirring]

248
17:52.302 --> 17:53.970
[loud bang]

249
18:13.448 --> 18:16.159
[gentle music continues playing]

250
18:36.262 --> 18:38.306
[gasps, chuckles]

251
18:39.474 --> 18:41.684
-Hey. -Hey. What's up?

252
18:41.768 --> 18:43.978
Oh, I just happened to be around.

253
18:44.062 --> 18:46.940
I had no idea Korea had so many traditional liquors.

254
18:47.523 --> 18:50.193
You're right. Can't believe there are so many.

255
18:52.987 --> 18:54.322
I don't recognize any of them.

256
18:55.490 --> 18:57.283
I've heard of soju and makgeolli.

257
18:57.367 --> 18:59.202
But there's Leegangju, gamhongnoju,

258
18:59.285 --> 19:03.122
Jindo hongju, Hansan sogokju, munbaeju, omegisul…

259
19:03.206 --> 19:05.667
-There are so many kinds. -Wow.

260
19:05.750 --> 19:07.126
The land of liquor, huh?

261
19:07.210 --> 19:08.211
[laughing]

262
19:11.297 --> 19:12.757
This one's over 40%.

263
19:12.840 --> 19:14.592
Yeah, it is.

264
19:17.845 --> 19:19.180
Hmm.

265
19:23.643 --> 19:25.561
Wait. Are you buying all that?

266
19:29.482 --> 19:33.152
I'm going to try them with some Korean food over dinner with the staff tonight.

267
19:33.945 --> 19:35.530
Oh. Look.

268
19:36.239 --> 19:40.034
Apparently, this is the hottest food delivery app in Korea right now.

269
19:40.118 --> 19:41.703
-It's a huge success. -Oh.

270
19:41.786 --> 19:43.079
They have everything.

271
19:43.162 --> 19:44.497
It's awesome.

272
19:44.580 --> 19:46.666
-Awesome? -Yeah.

273
19:49.168 --> 19:51.295
-Oh, this looks good. -Mm-hmm.

274
19:53.756 --> 19:55.675
Will you join us?

275
19:58.469 --> 19:59.762
Come on, let's try it together.

276
19:59.846 --> 20:02.015
Korean delivery food with traditional liquor.

277
20:03.057 --> 20:04.058
Hmm.

278
20:10.815 --> 20:11.941
[Han] A bit harder.

279
20:12.025 --> 20:15.611
Like I said before, you beat enough air into it.

280
20:31.461 --> 20:34.964
It isn't fully cooked yet, so it's okay to stir it like this.

281
20:35.965 --> 20:38.968
It must be cooked slowly over low heat. Don't forget that.

282
20:41.054 --> 20:44.223
Scrape around the edges, while tilting the pan.

283
20:45.266 --> 20:46.517
Here, now you try it.

284
20:50.396 --> 20:52.148
No, no, no. Not there.

285
20:52.231 --> 20:53.649
You can't touch that part anymore.

286
20:54.233 --> 20:57.487
It's already cooked enough, so if you touch it, it'll lose its shape.

287
20:58.237 --> 21:00.156
Now, sprinkle some cheese on it.

288
21:02.283 --> 21:05.536
It cooks very quickly from this point on, so you have to move fast.

289
21:05.620 --> 21:06.621
Okay?

290
21:07.663 --> 21:10.374
Tilt the pan as you slowly fold it over

291
21:10.458 --> 21:13.086
from the outside in, almost like you're rolling it, okay?

292
21:13.669 --> 21:15.671
Not like that. Bit by bit.

293
21:15.755 --> 21:16.964
No, uh, gently…

294
21:17.048 --> 21:18.049
Uh…

295
21:20.259 --> 21:21.344
Let's try again.

296
21:39.320 --> 21:40.321
Again.

297
21:41.489 --> 21:42.865
It's overcooked.

298
21:47.495 --> 21:49.372
I told you to tilt the pan more.

299
21:49.455 --> 21:50.665
Again.

300
21:57.296 --> 21:58.339
Stop.

301
22:04.595 --> 22:06.681
-Again. -Ugh, come on.

302
22:20.653 --> 22:21.654
Here, let me.

303
22:35.251 --> 22:36.335
Okay.

304
22:47.889 --> 22:49.140
Not easy, is it?

305
22:49.223 --> 22:52.310
An omelet looks easy to make, but it's tricky to get it right.

306
22:52.894 --> 22:54.145
You're using a spatula now,

307
22:54.228 --> 22:56.981
but you must be able to use chopsticks too.

308
22:57.940 --> 22:58.941
Remember.

309
22:59.025 --> 23:00.818
Practice and more practice.

310
23:04.155 --> 23:05.281
[sighs]

311
23:08.993 --> 23:10.119
Song.

312
23:10.203 --> 23:12.079
Don't be too disappointed.

313
23:12.788 --> 23:15.291
Making an omelet is harder than it actually looks.

314
23:15.374 --> 23:16.417
At first, everyone--

315
23:21.130 --> 23:22.298
I'm sorry.

316
23:22.381 --> 23:23.758
I'm going to get some air.

317
23:29.055 --> 23:30.097
[door slams]

318
23:42.193 --> 23:43.778
[gentle music playing]

319
23:43.861 --> 23:44.862
[sighs]

320
24:05.383 --> 24:09.053
The women in my family have no talent for cooking at all.

321
24:11.764 --> 24:14.225
My mom told me that when I was little.

322
24:14.308 --> 24:16.435
She wasn't a very good cook either.

323
24:18.729 --> 24:20.231
Mmm.

324
24:21.565 --> 24:26.570
So, most of the food I remember from growing up was made by my father actually.

325
24:27.822 --> 24:29.532
Not just Western food.

326
24:30.491 --> 24:33.369
Doenjang jjigae, kimchi jjim,

327
24:33.452 --> 24:35.621
duruchigi, bibimbap,

328
24:36.455 --> 24:37.915
namul side dishes.

329
24:38.833 --> 24:39.834
Yeah.

330
24:43.629 --> 24:45.298
Maybe I take after my mom.

331
24:45.923 --> 24:48.301
I don't seem to have what it takes either.

332
24:51.929 --> 24:53.431
And on top of that,

333
24:54.181 --> 24:57.184
people have always said I shouldn't even be allowed in the kitchen.

334
24:58.477 --> 25:01.147
Apparently, the ghost on my shoulder goes berserk

335
25:01.230 --> 25:03.399
whenever it sees fire or something.

336
25:07.194 --> 25:10.614
They said other people would get hurt pretty badly if I went into the kitchen.

337
25:12.408 --> 25:13.993
Because I've been cursed.

338
25:17.538 --> 25:19.623
It sounds ridiculous, right?

339
25:20.750 --> 25:22.126
But…

340
25:23.753 --> 25:26.047
people really did get hurt whenever I did it.

341
25:27.840 --> 25:29.008
Even my dad.

342
25:33.179 --> 25:34.180
Chris.

343
25:38.559 --> 25:40.561
I'm no help for you guys here.

344
25:41.312 --> 25:43.022
I'll only get in the way.

345
25:45.691 --> 25:47.651
And no matter how hard you try…

346
25:50.279 --> 25:52.031
I won't get any better.

347
25:55.618 --> 25:58.245
I don't deserve to be a part of this team.

348
26:04.335 --> 26:05.628
If someone

349
26:06.796 --> 26:08.422
were to get hurt because of me…

350
26:09.965 --> 26:10.966
[sniffs]

351
26:12.218 --> 26:15.388
If someone were to actually get hurt because of me…

352
26:29.443 --> 26:31.278
I know how you feel right now.

353
26:33.614 --> 26:35.699
I also know that nothing I say

354
26:35.783 --> 26:37.326
will actually reach you.

355
26:41.080 --> 26:42.748
I was the same way at first.

356
26:48.045 --> 26:49.046
Song.

357
26:50.548 --> 26:54.427
Cooking isn't about luck. It's science.

358
26:55.010 --> 26:57.221
Ghosts and curses have nothing to do with it.

359
26:58.097 --> 27:00.891
There's only repetition and practice.

360
27:00.975 --> 27:01.976
Hmm?

361
27:06.188 --> 27:08.357
Whatever has happened to you in the past,

362
27:09.483 --> 27:11.652
whatever people have told you,

363
27:11.735 --> 27:13.404
remember just one thing.

364
27:16.657 --> 27:18.909
You mustn't try to run away from

365
27:19.577 --> 27:22.663
or forget everything that's happened in your life.

366
27:26.459 --> 27:31.922
Because a life you turn away from can never truly be yours.

367
27:34.842 --> 27:36.510
[sniffles]

368
27:39.930 --> 27:41.182
I'm not giving up.

369
27:42.183 --> 27:45.769
Not on you, not on Famiglia, not on the prize.

370
27:51.066 --> 27:52.234
So, Song.

371
27:53.027 --> 27:54.820
Do not let go.

372
27:54.904 --> 27:56.530
Let's not give up here.

373
27:59.617 --> 28:01.118
[sniffles, chuckles]

374
28:03.787 --> 28:04.788
All right.

375
28:04.872 --> 28:05.873
[grunts softly]

376
28:08.751 --> 28:10.461
In order to make a good omelet,

377
28:11.045 --> 28:12.755
you need to beat the eggs well first.

378
28:12.838 --> 28:15.549
It's also important to season them properly.

379
28:15.633 --> 28:19.261
But what matters most is heat control and knowing when to roll it.

380
28:19.345 --> 28:21.764
If you mess these up, it'll be all for naught.

381
28:24.099 --> 28:25.392
The rest is time.

382
28:25.476 --> 28:26.810
Time will take care of it.

383
28:27.686 --> 28:31.815
We'll practice two or three more times, and then we'll start your palate training.

384
28:34.985 --> 28:35.819
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026 ROUND 3

385
28:35.903 --> 28:37.988
HAEON COUNTY, THE SOUTHERNMOST TIP OF KOREA

386
28:38.072 --> 28:40.407
[no audible dialogue]

387
28:42.284 --> 28:43.494
HAEON ELEMENTARY SCHOOL

388
28:47.039 --> 28:48.249
YOU ARE MY DESTINY

389
28:48.332 --> 28:49.667
ROUND 3 - WITH HAEON ELEMENTARY SCHOOL GRADUATES

390
28:49.750 --> 28:51.210
OUTDOOR STAGE - A SPECIAL KITCHEN BUILT ON THE FIELD

391
28:51.293 --> 28:52.962
COLLABORATIVE WORK

392
28:53.045 --> 28:54.547
RANDOM DRAW

393
28:54.630 --> 28:57.216
[no audible dialogue]

394
28:59.635 --> 29:01.220
[Hyeon-ju] At first,

395
29:01.303 --> 29:04.348
I thought the theme was actually kind of cheesy.

396
29:04.431 --> 29:06.684
"You Are My Destiny."

397
29:07.268 --> 29:08.686
That thing called destiny…

398
29:11.730 --> 29:13.232
that's a word

399
29:13.315 --> 29:16.819
we usually use for married couples or parents and children.

400
29:16.902 --> 29:18.612
But I do wonder… [inhales sharply]

401
29:18.696 --> 29:20.948
…whether food can also be a matter of destiny

402
29:21.031 --> 29:23.534
or if it's actually a stretch to even consider it.

403
29:23.617 --> 29:25.661
Of course, I know nothing about cooking,

404
29:25.744 --> 29:27.871
but for people who've devoted their lives to food,

405
29:27.955 --> 29:29.540
your husband…

406
29:34.587 --> 29:37.965
He actually was an incredible Korean cuisine chef.

407
29:38.048 --> 29:39.425
What was his name again?

408
29:40.175 --> 29:42.845
Was it Kang San? And the son…

409
29:48.017 --> 29:51.186
I'm sorry for bringing it up.

410
29:51.270 --> 29:53.856
This is the problem with having such a good memory.

411
29:53.939 --> 29:56.900
Geez. That's taboo at Pyeongyeon Group.

412
29:56.984 --> 29:58.777
I ought to just stitch my mouth shut.

413
30:02.865 --> 30:04.408
I'VE ATTACHED MATERIALS ON CHRIS K. RESTAURANTS

414
30:04.491 --> 30:06.619
RESTAURANTS WITH CHRIS K. FULLY BOOKED 6 MONTHS AHEAD

415
30:09.455 --> 30:10.831
IN NEW YORK'S FINE-DINING INDUSTRY, CHRIS K.…

416
30:12.499 --> 30:14.668
NEW YORK'S CULINARY WORLD TAKES NOTICE OF AN ASIAN CHEF

417
30:16.420 --> 30:18.255
SOUS-CHEF MORE FAMOUS THAN THE HEAD CHEF…

418
30:19.465 --> 30:20.674
ONE BITE, AND I UNDERSTOOD THE HYPE

419
30:20.758 --> 30:21.967
EVERYTHING ELSE SEEMS BLAND NOW

420
30:23.761 --> 30:25.262
INTERVIEWS, RESTAURANT REVIEWS, ACADEMIC RECORDS

421
30:34.313 --> 30:36.398
NO RECORDS FROM BEFORE HIGH SCHOOL COULD BE FOUND

422
30:47.201 --> 30:48.535
[inhales sharply] Level three.

423
30:49.495 --> 30:50.496
No, no.

424
30:51.455 --> 30:52.748
It's not level four either.

425
30:53.415 --> 30:56.168
It's somewhere between level three and level four.

426
30:57.044 --> 30:58.420
Isn't it level three

427
30:59.129 --> 31:01.340
with just a pinch of extra salt?

428
31:07.096 --> 31:08.472
-Chris. -Huh?

429
31:08.555 --> 31:09.890
What level is it?

430
31:09.973 --> 31:11.975
[stammers] You're right.

431
31:12.935 --> 31:14.478
It's between levels three and four.

432
31:15.145 --> 31:17.606
I added about 50 milligrams to level three.

433
31:18.190 --> 31:20.776
-But how-- -Yes! [giggles]

434
31:21.276 --> 31:24.363
I knew it. You put that in on purpose to trip me up, didn't you?

435
31:24.446 --> 31:28.033
But I got them all right. Can't fool me, can you? [giggles]

436
31:31.412 --> 31:32.871
This is crazy.

437
31:33.664 --> 31:34.665
Song.

438
31:35.332 --> 31:36.333
Yes?

439
31:36.417 --> 31:38.419
You're the first person to both distinguish

440
31:39.420 --> 31:41.547
all ten levels of saltiness and catch on to my trick.

441
31:43.465 --> 31:44.466
This is…

442
31:47.970 --> 31:48.971
Song.

443
31:49.930 --> 31:52.099
Song, you have an incredible gift.

444
31:52.182 --> 31:54.518
One no other chef in the world has.

445
31:55.144 --> 31:56.145
[chuckles]

446
31:56.979 --> 31:58.480
Let's practice some more.

447
31:58.564 --> 32:00.399
With the flavors and aromas of herbs.

448
32:01.150 --> 32:02.151
Wait here.

449
32:12.911 --> 32:13.912
Chairwoman?

450
32:14.913 --> 32:17.416
[Hae-seon] Are you busy? Can you talk right now?

451
32:17.499 --> 32:20.669
Oh, it's fine. We just wrapped up lunch.

452
32:21.670 --> 32:22.755
I see.

453
32:28.469 --> 32:30.554
Is anything wrong?

454
32:33.432 --> 32:36.769
Hwang brought back some barley-aged dried yellow croaker from vacation.

455
32:36.852 --> 32:37.936
It looks delicious.

456
32:39.354 --> 32:40.647
Can you come over for dinner?

457
32:40.731 --> 32:43.358
We haven't had dinner together in a while.

458
32:45.778 --> 32:47.946
I've already cleared it with Reporter Park.

459
32:48.030 --> 32:49.948
Serve them each a pre-dinner cocktail.

460
32:50.032 --> 32:52.367
-And a bottle of champagne on the house. -Yes, Chef.

461
32:52.451 --> 32:55.704
And don't forget to tell them it's a gift, so they shouldn't feel obligated.

462
32:55.788 --> 32:57.748
-Understood. Have a good evening. -Thanks.

463
33:17.768 --> 33:20.187
Hey, Mark. Come on. Why so quiet tonight?

464
33:20.729 --> 33:22.606
Come on. Don't think about the competition.

465
33:22.689 --> 33:24.191
Just drink.

466
33:24.274 --> 33:29.321
Yeah. Tomorrow's another day, sous-chef. Come on. Let's have some fun, huh?

467
33:30.447 --> 33:32.241
Hey, man. This is really awesome.

468
33:32.991 --> 33:34.576
Yeah. Yeah, Ron.

469
33:34.660 --> 33:35.702
Everybody, listen.

470
33:36.745 --> 33:39.081
We're going to drink this all tonight.

471
33:39.623 --> 33:40.874
Okay?

472
33:40.958 --> 33:43.627
-[Ron] Let's do it. -Okay.

473
33:44.586 --> 33:46.255
Let's drink it and go to hell.

474
33:46.338 --> 33:47.422
To hell.

475
33:51.051 --> 33:52.469
[groaning]

476
33:52.553 --> 33:54.388
-[groans] -[Stanley] That's strong.

477
33:54.471 --> 33:56.598
You've got to try it with this chicken.

478
33:56.682 --> 33:59.059
-[Ron] Mmm. Was that chicken? -[Stanley] Yeah.

479
33:59.142 --> 34:00.644
I don't know what it's called though.

480
34:01.395 --> 34:03.856
-I haven't tried the tteokbokki yet. -[doorbell rings]

481
34:07.818 --> 34:09.403
Isabel. I'm glad you're here.

482
34:10.612 --> 34:11.738
[sighs]

483
34:30.299 --> 34:31.592
[Hae-seon] I invited her.

484
34:32.259 --> 34:34.094
She's been working so hard lately.

485
34:35.137 --> 34:37.806
It's been a while since you two had a home-cooked meal, hasn't it?

486
34:39.266 --> 34:40.517
Yeah.

487
34:41.184 --> 34:42.769
[Hae-seon] Come on in.

488
34:48.108 --> 34:50.569
I don't know if it'll suit your tastes.

489
34:50.652 --> 34:52.529
It's seasoned to my old taste buds.

490
34:52.613 --> 34:55.407
Not at all. It's delicious, Chairwoman.

491
34:55.490 --> 34:57.367
-[chuckles] -I agree. It's delicious.

492
34:57.451 --> 34:58.744
I'm glad.

493
34:58.827 --> 35:00.787
I was worried you might not like it.

494
35:01.288 --> 35:02.789
Take your time and help yourselves.

495
35:03.790 --> 35:04.791
Yes, Chairwoman.

496
35:07.002 --> 35:09.755
You know you don't have to keep calling me that when we're at home.

497
35:11.715 --> 35:12.716
I'm sorry?

498
35:14.468 --> 35:15.677
Oh.

499
35:16.595 --> 35:17.846
Understood, Chair…

500
35:18.764 --> 35:19.973
-[chuckles] -I mean… [chuckles]

501
35:21.808 --> 35:23.060
Yes, understood.

502
35:29.566 --> 35:30.734
As I get older,

503
35:31.568 --> 35:34.363
my tastes seem to become more like a child's.

504
35:34.988 --> 35:36.198
I used to prefer

505
35:36.782 --> 35:39.451
eating barley-aged dried yellow croaker plain,

506
35:39.534 --> 35:40.744
but as the years go by,

507
35:40.827 --> 35:44.706
I find myself liking it more and more dipped in fried gochujang.

508
35:46.583 --> 35:49.544
Maybe it reminds me of my childhood, when I preferred stronger flavors.

509
35:49.628 --> 35:51.380
Or my palate is getting dull,

510
35:51.463 --> 35:53.715
so I'm seeking out stronger flavors.

511
35:55.676 --> 35:57.594
[chuckles]

512
35:58.512 --> 36:00.138
"You Are My Destiny," huh?

513
36:01.598 --> 36:02.849
When I was young,

514
36:04.267 --> 36:07.354
I believed that my dream was my destiny.

515
36:07.938 --> 36:09.147
Then at some point,

516
36:09.982 --> 36:11.817
I believed my family was my destiny.

517
36:14.152 --> 36:16.947
Now my dream and my family are gone.

518
36:19.950 --> 36:21.410
So what is my destiny?

519
36:32.421 --> 36:33.422
Chairwoman.

520
36:37.175 --> 36:41.179
From what I remember, you spent your childhood in Haeon County, didn't you?

521
36:41.805 --> 36:45.684
And you graduated from Haeon Elementary, where we're holding the next round.

522
36:47.728 --> 36:49.021
Yes, I did.

523
36:55.110 --> 36:56.278
Then, for this round,

524
36:57.904 --> 37:00.907
how about you come along with us and take part as a judge?

525
37:06.747 --> 37:08.248
As a judge?

526
37:24.806 --> 37:26.391
When do you fly out?

527
37:27.601 --> 37:29.061
The morning after tomorrow.

528
37:31.980 --> 37:35.734
[sighs] At least being eliminated early gave me a chance to travel around Korea.

529
37:36.443 --> 37:38.945
I feel like I've gotten to know Korea a little better now.

530
37:39.905 --> 37:42.407
Hmm. Well, there's still a lot I don't know yet.

531
37:44.242 --> 37:48.497
I'm a little jealous you got to relax and enjoy Korea before you go home.

532
37:49.873 --> 37:51.833
I kind of wish I'd been eliminated early too.

533
37:52.959 --> 37:54.920
[both laughing]

534
37:58.757 --> 38:00.550
How do you like the liquor?

535
38:00.634 --> 38:02.094
Hmm…

536
38:02.177 --> 38:03.845
Harsh, but…

537
38:05.055 --> 38:06.640
better than I expected.

538
38:06.723 --> 38:09.601
Since they're usually made by fermenting grains like rice,

539
38:09.684 --> 38:11.561
they don't have particularly rich aromas or bouquets,

540
38:11.645 --> 38:12.938
but how should I put it?

541
38:14.731 --> 38:17.442
Hmm. They taste really clean.

542
38:18.401 --> 38:21.863
Kind of like a very sharp knife cutting clean through something.

543
38:23.198 --> 38:25.867
Like it makes you completely forget what you just ate.

544
38:26.785 --> 38:27.869
Sort of that?

545
38:27.953 --> 38:29.704
[both chuckling]

546
38:33.959 --> 38:39.381
-[coughing] Holy cow. -[laughing]

547
38:42.008 --> 38:43.885
-It is harsh. -It is.

548
38:43.969 --> 38:45.554
-[coughing continues] -[pats back]

549
38:45.637 --> 38:46.888
-You okay? -Yeah.

550
38:49.391 --> 38:52.853
-Oh! Wow. -Oh. Ooh.

551
38:54.563 --> 38:56.148
[both sigh]

552
38:59.109 --> 39:02.320
Whenever you are in the States,

553
39:03.405 --> 39:04.447
come to Charleston.

554
39:05.907 --> 39:07.492
Yeah, I will. Sure.

555
39:11.621 --> 39:12.622
Joshua.

556
39:14.958 --> 39:18.295
I really hope that it's you who wins this competition.

557
39:19.337 --> 39:20.630
I mean it.

558
39:20.714 --> 39:22.174
[gentle music playing]

559
39:22.257 --> 39:24.885
And whatever it is you came here looking for…

560
39:27.137 --> 39:28.638
I hope you find it.

561
39:53.496 --> 39:54.623
[clattering]

562
40:05.467 --> 40:06.885
[objects rustling]

563
40:14.559 --> 40:16.311
What are you doing so early?

564
40:17.312 --> 40:18.355
Hey, Song.

565
40:19.648 --> 40:23.235
[chuckles] I'm just heading to a nearby mountain.

566
40:23.318 --> 40:24.778
And I'll stop by a campground.

567
40:25.570 --> 40:27.781
By yourself? Really?

568
40:28.740 --> 40:32.118
You're going camping when the next round's just around the corner?

569
40:34.037 --> 40:35.288
The restaurant's closed today.

570
40:35.372 --> 40:37.624
I can take a day to clear my head, right?

571
40:38.500 --> 40:42.170
Besides… [sighs] …we'll be away for five whole days for this round.

572
40:43.713 --> 40:45.465
Don't worry. I'll be back by dawn.

573
40:47.342 --> 40:51.346
Oh, and you too. Take the day off, okay?

574
40:51.429 --> 40:52.430
[chuckles]

575
40:54.307 --> 40:55.308
Mmm. Okay.

576
41:10.115 --> 41:12.367
[emotional music playing]

577
41:12.450 --> 41:13.785
-Can I-- -Would you like--

578
41:22.585 --> 41:25.588
Do you think I could go with you, perhaps?

579
41:27.841 --> 41:31.303
I mean, I don't really have anything to do here by myself.

580
41:31.845 --> 41:34.055
And I could use some fresh air for once.

581
41:35.432 --> 41:39.019
I can get some cooking practice in while we make food at the campground,

582
41:39.102 --> 41:40.937
and, uh, it'll be easier to get there in my truck.

583
41:41.021 --> 41:44.566
It's like they say, two birds with one stone.

584
41:46.776 --> 41:47.777
[chuckles]

585
41:48.278 --> 41:49.446
All right.

586
41:55.076 --> 41:56.077
[Song-yi groans]

587
41:56.161 --> 41:58.455
[mystical music playing]

588
41:58.538 --> 42:00.749
-[Han chuckles] -[Song-yi sighs]

589
42:02.208 --> 42:03.460
[whining] Chris.

590
42:04.377 --> 42:07.047
You said we were going camping, not hiking.

591
42:34.324 --> 42:35.325
Hmm?

592
42:43.583 --> 42:44.584
Oh.

593
43:18.701 --> 43:19.702
There.

594
43:23.415 --> 43:24.416
Let's go.

595
43:31.172 --> 43:32.173
[chuckles]

596
43:36.010 --> 43:37.011
Take my hand.

597
43:40.265 --> 43:41.599
It'll be easier if you do.

598
43:43.309 --> 43:44.602
Come on.

599
43:44.686 --> 43:46.688
[upbeat music playing]

600
43:49.524 --> 43:51.359
Come on, hurry, let's go.

601
43:51.443 --> 43:52.777
[Song-yi] Oh. Oh.

602
44:30.356 --> 44:32.775
[groans, spits]

603
44:33.818 --> 44:34.819
Ew, what is this?

604
44:34.903 --> 44:36.863
Why does it sting and taste so bitter?

605
44:39.574 --> 44:40.575
You swallowed it?

606
44:41.451 --> 44:43.453
You can't just put anything in your mouth.

607
44:44.245 --> 44:45.246
[grunts]

608
44:46.039 --> 44:47.624
Here. Rinse your mouth, quick.

609
44:49.292 --> 44:50.293
[gags]

610
44:52.795 --> 44:55.131
[spits, groans]

611
44:55.215 --> 44:56.799
What on earth was that?

612
44:56.883 --> 44:59.469
-Why does it sting so much? -It's poisonous.

613
44:59.552 --> 45:01.346
What? Poisonous?

614
45:01.429 --> 45:02.722
Don't worry too much.

615
45:03.264 --> 45:05.391
That amount isn't enough to do serious harm.

616
45:06.684 --> 45:08.186
But you have to be careful.

617
45:08.978 --> 45:11.856
Even a thumb-sized amount can cause blindness.

618
45:13.149 --> 45:15.735
Why on earth are you collecting poisonous plants like that?

619
45:15.818 --> 45:18.071
What if someone eats it and something bad happens?

620
45:18.780 --> 45:19.781
Hold on.

621
45:20.573 --> 45:22.992
You're not thinking of doing something bad, are you?

622
45:23.076 --> 45:24.327
[scoffs]

623
45:24.410 --> 45:25.453
Sorry?

624
45:27.330 --> 45:29.499
Don't tell me, these are all poisonous.

625
45:30.500 --> 45:32.460
No. The two of these aren't.

626
45:32.544 --> 45:33.962
It's all poisonous…

627
45:35.588 --> 45:38.591
Are you crazy, Chris? Are you trying to get someone killed?

628
45:38.675 --> 45:41.386
You can't take this many dangerous plants back home with you!

629
45:42.011 --> 45:43.972
No, but I'll keep them out of reach.

630
45:44.055 --> 45:46.057
I mean, even so. [grunts]

631
45:46.140 --> 45:48.226
You can't lug around this many dangerous plants with you.

632
45:48.309 --> 45:50.228
-I'm throwing them all away. -No, no, no. Don't, don't.

633
45:50.311 --> 45:51.312
I need all of these.

634
45:51.396 --> 45:53.940
Why would you need something so dangerous? Hand them over.

635
45:54.023 --> 45:55.984
It took me ages to collect them.

636
45:56.067 --> 45:58.319
-Hand them over. They're really dangerous. -No. No way.

637
45:58.403 --> 46:00.572
-Give them to me. You said it yourself. -Hey! No. No! I said no.

638
46:00.655 --> 46:02.782
-They're poisonous! Chris! -No!

639
46:02.865 --> 46:05.493
-[knocking on door] -[Stanley] Joshua. Joshua?

640
46:05.577 --> 46:06.911
Open the door.

641
46:08.037 --> 46:09.038
Joshua.

642
46:11.457 --> 46:12.458
Joshua.

643
46:13.126 --> 46:16.254
Joshua? Open the door. Joshua.

644
46:18.131 --> 46:19.299
Joshua.

645
46:19.382 --> 46:20.508
We got a problem.

646
46:23.344 --> 46:24.804
[door closes]

647
46:25.638 --> 46:28.099
Oh, I'm sorry. I got up late.

648
46:29.976 --> 46:31.060
What's wrong?

649
46:33.438 --> 46:34.439
Joshua.

650
46:36.774 --> 46:39.360
[Mark] My girlfriend said she's leaving me.

651
46:39.444 --> 46:41.654
I think she got sick of waiting for me.

652
46:41.738 --> 46:44.157
You guys know that I can't live without her.

653
46:44.240 --> 46:47.327
I'm so sorry, but I need to go back to the States.

654
46:47.952 --> 46:50.038
Spineless little rat.

655
46:50.830 --> 46:52.540
I knew it.

656
46:53.374 --> 46:56.127
Now it makes sense why he was always so nervous.

657
47:00.173 --> 47:03.051
What are we going to do now, Joshua? Huh?

658
47:06.596 --> 47:09.515
[grunts, breathes deeply]

659
47:10.058 --> 47:13.478
This idiot got eliminated for preparing puffer fish soup.

660
47:14.062 --> 47:15.063
Hmm.

661
47:16.064 --> 47:17.690
[suspenseful music playing]

662
47:22.236 --> 47:25.865
Oh, her! It was a shame to lose her! Koo, look!

663
47:25.948 --> 47:28.785
A pretty face, a hot bod…

664
47:28.868 --> 47:30.328
The audience really liked her.

665
47:30.411 --> 47:32.121
Well, geez. [clicks tongue]

666
47:32.205 --> 47:34.040
She got eliminated way too early.

667
47:36.167 --> 47:37.960
[grunts, sighs]

668
47:39.671 --> 47:42.048
Let's see, let's see, let's see, let's see,

669
47:42.131 --> 47:43.966
let's see, let's see, let's see.

670
47:44.926 --> 47:45.927
Aha.

671
47:47.220 --> 47:51.182
If this one wins the contest, she can't hand the company over to him.

672
47:51.265 --> 47:52.892
Shh.

673
47:53.851 --> 47:55.061
And if this one wins,

674
47:55.144 --> 47:58.940
she'll be accused of trying to make her secret son the winner of the contest.

675
48:01.109 --> 48:02.235
Checkmate.

676
48:02.318 --> 48:03.695
She's boxed in.

677
48:03.778 --> 48:05.488
[shouts] If so,

678
48:05.571 --> 48:06.614
which of these…

679
48:06.698 --> 48:10.493
[singsongy] …knife-wielders am I supposed to make the winner?

680
48:10.576 --> 48:12.245
Geez, this is giving me a headache! Ah!

681
48:12.328 --> 48:13.830
I ought to just…

682
48:13.913 --> 48:17.125
[grunting]

683
48:17.208 --> 48:18.209
Moon Hae-seon.

684
48:19.001 --> 48:21.379
Yeah. Moon Hae-seon!

685
48:23.047 --> 48:24.632
Damn you.

686
48:24.716 --> 48:25.967
[exhales deeply]

687
48:28.052 --> 48:30.430
You. I don't like you.

688
48:30.513 --> 48:32.014
I really don't like you.

689
48:33.057 --> 48:37.562
But you're useful, so I suppose I have to keep you alive, right?

690
48:39.522 --> 48:40.690
More importantly!

691
48:40.773 --> 48:43.359
I really don't like this old French bastard!

692
48:43.443 --> 48:44.902
I feel like he's up to something.

693
48:44.986 --> 48:47.864
Like he knows something, but is pretending he doesn't.

694
48:47.947 --> 48:50.575
He just gives me this weird, unpleasant feeling.

695
48:50.658 --> 48:53.119
And he even looks like a damn mutt.

696
48:53.202 --> 48:54.829
[sniffs] Damn it!

697
48:54.912 --> 48:58.583
Not to mention that weird cologne he wears. Well, I'll be… [grunts]

698
49:00.168 --> 49:01.711
[gasps]

699
49:01.794 --> 49:03.463
Round Three is underway.

700
49:04.213 --> 49:07.175
-How about we start warming up too? -Okay.

701
49:07.258 --> 49:10.845
-What should we start with? -[stammers]

702
49:15.600 --> 49:17.226
What should we give him?

703
49:19.437 --> 49:21.773
[Han] Innate talent. Sharp instincts.

704
49:22.565 --> 49:23.941
I had none of those things.

705
49:25.651 --> 49:27.820
It was a new challenge every time.

706
49:29.322 --> 49:33.367
Starting from scratch, learning, struggling, getting discouraged,

707
49:34.327 --> 49:35.953
then starting all over again…

708
49:37.538 --> 49:39.040
and failing again.

709
49:42.668 --> 49:43.836
But people don't really

710
49:45.087 --> 49:46.464
care to understand

711
49:47.673 --> 49:49.258
how the process goes.

712
50:02.230 --> 50:03.231
Listen…

713
50:04.482 --> 50:05.900
can I ask you something?

714
50:07.777 --> 50:11.447
What exactly does this competition mean to you, Chris?

715
50:12.365 --> 50:15.701
You still haven't told me why you suddenly changed your mind

716
50:15.785 --> 50:18.454
and decided to enter the competition and to help us.

717
50:18.538 --> 50:20.122
I really don't understand.

718
50:20.206 --> 50:22.625
What brought on the sudden change of heart?

719
50:24.877 --> 50:26.838
[gentle music playing]

720
50:31.968 --> 50:33.261
Hmm.

721
50:35.638 --> 50:37.849
That day you first came to Famiglia.

722
50:38.724 --> 50:40.768
Remember what you told me in the kitchen?

723
50:41.394 --> 50:45.898
You said cooking isn't simply about serving delicious food to customers.

724
50:47.525 --> 50:50.486
And that food can bring back someone's precious memories,

725
50:51.612 --> 50:52.822
and even give them

726
50:54.532 --> 50:56.617
the courage to keep going.

727
51:01.789 --> 51:03.499
And that's what Famiglia…

728
51:04.834 --> 51:07.461
That's what it and its food mean to me.

729
51:09.547 --> 51:10.590
That's why…

730
51:12.258 --> 51:13.426
I really want

731
51:14.427 --> 51:16.345
to win this competition.

732
51:18.264 --> 51:19.599
Even if

733
51:20.182 --> 51:22.351
I'm not capable of running Famiglia,

734
51:22.435 --> 51:26.147
even if I have no talent for cooking at all,

735
51:26.230 --> 51:29.483
even if I'm cursed to stay out of the kitchen, I still…

736
51:30.443 --> 51:32.445
really want to win.

737
51:33.529 --> 51:34.739
I want to beat Pyeongyeon Group,

738
51:34.822 --> 51:36.699
the company that drove my father to his death.

739
51:48.920 --> 51:50.129
Want to know a secret?

740
51:50.755 --> 51:51.839
Hmm?

741
51:53.674 --> 51:54.675
You see, I…

742
51:55.760 --> 51:59.430
I only have one-third of my sense of smell left.

743
52:00.222 --> 52:01.223
What?

744
52:01.307 --> 52:03.142
Part of it is genetic,

745
52:04.352 --> 52:06.729
but when I was young, I ate, um,

746
52:06.812 --> 52:09.023
a poisonous plant by accident.

747
52:09.899 --> 52:10.942
But then…

748
52:12.360 --> 52:13.945
how can you…

749
52:15.237 --> 52:18.824
How can you identify aromas and season food accurately

750
52:18.908 --> 52:21.410
with so little of your sense of smell left?

751
52:22.870 --> 52:24.455
Who knows?

752
52:24.538 --> 52:26.415
How do you think I do it?

753
52:29.627 --> 52:30.628
Destiny.

754
52:32.088 --> 52:33.839
[mysterious music playing]

755
52:35.174 --> 52:37.009
I just think of it as destiny.

756
52:39.887 --> 52:43.224
As if it were inescapable.

757
52:47.436 --> 52:48.854
The how comes later.

758
52:50.106 --> 52:51.440
Whatever it may be.

759
52:51.524 --> 52:53.150
[upbeat music playing]

760
52:54.986 --> 52:56.362
Then I just believe…

761
52:58.447 --> 53:01.909
I can shape that destiny however I want.

762
53:26.017 --> 53:28.519
[emotional music playing]

763
53:36.152 --> 53:37.903
YOU ARE MY DESTINY THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026

764
53:40.406 --> 53:42.033
[intense music playing]

765
53:47.663 --> 53:48.998
[no audible dialogue]

766
53:49.081 --> 53:51.876
I mean it. It's not the best of situations.

767
53:51.959 --> 53:54.128
[Captain Cook] The venue for this competition is Haeon,

768
53:55.212 --> 53:58.257
at the very south of Korea.

769
54:02.636 --> 54:05.347
For your convenience, we've prepared three vehicles,

770
54:05.431 --> 54:07.099
each in a different color.

771
54:07.183 --> 54:11.020
Two chefs, each from one team, will share a vehicle.

772
54:11.103 --> 54:13.481
Oh, but don't worry too much.

773
54:13.564 --> 54:17.068
The rest of your team will follow on a bus right after you.

774
54:19.612 --> 54:24.742
Each one of the vehicles will have a different hint related to the challenge.

775
54:26.327 --> 54:30.456
Which hint you get will solely depend on the vehicle you choose.

776
54:31.499 --> 54:33.626
The number you select is the number of the vehicle

777
54:33.709 --> 54:36.587
that you'll ride in for this round.

778
54:37.797 --> 54:41.383
Your order is determined by the number on the slip

779
54:42.259 --> 54:44.887
you drew when you entered this meeting room earlier.

780
55:08.494 --> 55:10.204
[door unlocks]

781
55:10.287 --> 55:13.040
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026

782
55:26.512 --> 55:28.305
[intense music continues playing]

783
55:35.146 --> 55:36.522
[door unlocks]

784
55:52.872 --> 55:54.456
[door unlocks]

785
56:18.272 --> 56:20.232
[Woo-jin] There aren't any cameras in here.

786
56:49.762 --> 56:51.222
[door unlocks]

787
56:55.851 --> 56:56.852
[door closes]

788
57:12.201 --> 57:13.827
[sighs]

789
57:23.295 --> 57:25.923
[intense music continues playing]

790
58:41.332 --> 58:43.208
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026

791
58:50.341 --> 58:51.342
Where are we?

792
58:52.968 --> 58:54.970
-[chef 1] Did we come to the wrong place? -[chef 2] There's nothing here.

793
58:55.054 --> 58:57.056
[Captain Cook] The two of you riding in the same vehicle

794
58:57.765 --> 59:00.267
will be partners for this round.

795
59:03.145 --> 59:05.397
You will compete against others as a team.

796
59:06.357 --> 59:10.611
For this challenge, two opposing head chefs will pair up for the round.

797
59:10.694 --> 59:14.323
As the theme says, "You Are My Destiny."

798
59:15.032 --> 59:16.033
[scoffs]

799
59:17.368 --> 59:18.869
[Captain Cook] With a plus one, that is.

800
59:18.952 --> 59:23.207
Each head chef can call in exactly one additional person from their team.

801
59:23.290 --> 59:25.084
Only one person.

802
59:25.167 --> 59:28.087
[staff] Just one person from each team will be selected.

803
59:28.170 --> 59:32.049
Only the one person chosen by the head chef will travel to Haeon

804
59:32.132 --> 59:34.635
and compete alongside all the head chefs in this round.

805
59:34.718 --> 59:36.845
I mean, what on earth…

806
59:36.929 --> 59:39.223
-[sighs] -What? Just one of us?

807
59:42.393 --> 59:45.229
[Captain Cook] Now, choose your team member very carefully

808
59:45.312 --> 59:48.565
and… and then send a message to the chosen member.

809
59:53.570 --> 59:57.366
The message you will send will simply read, "You Are My Destiny."

810
59:57.449 --> 59:59.952
If you receive the message sent by your head chef,

811
01:00:00.035 --> 01:00:01.829
you must raise your hand immediately.

812
01:00:08.502 --> 01:00:09.503
[phone chimes]

813
01:00:14.591 --> 01:00:16.635
-[chef 3] What the… -[chef 4] Looks like she got it.

814
01:00:52.129 --> 01:00:53.297
[sighs]

815
01:00:56.800 --> 01:00:57.926
[Joshua] Please, Isabel.

816
01:00:59.845 --> 01:01:01.680
Now that our sous-chef has left,

817
01:01:02.473 --> 01:01:04.016
I'd like you to replace him.

818
01:01:06.685 --> 01:01:08.103
For the remaining rounds,

819
01:01:09.897 --> 01:01:11.273
please be my teammate.

820
01:01:13.901 --> 01:01:15.736
-[phone chimes] -[stammers] I…

821
01:01:17.404 --> 01:01:18.405
[scoffs]

822
01:01:20.699 --> 01:01:21.700
[clears throat]

823
01:01:23.327 --> 01:01:24.328
[chuckles]

824
01:01:26.038 --> 01:01:27.331
[phone chimes]

825
01:01:32.544 --> 01:01:33.921
[phone chimes]

826
01:01:51.813 --> 01:01:53.565
Good luck, Chef Geon-woo.

827
01:01:55.108 --> 01:01:56.777
You've got this.

828
01:01:56.860 --> 01:02:00.197
-[gasps] -Oh, Geon-woo, right…

829
01:02:00.280 --> 01:02:02.741
Chris will take care of everything, so don't worry too much.

830
01:02:02.824 --> 01:02:03.825
[both chuckle]

831
01:02:04.826 --> 01:02:06.161
Right.

832
01:02:09.164 --> 01:02:11.041
[phone chimes]

833
01:02:18.966 --> 01:02:20.759
[chef 5] This won't be easy.

834
01:02:37.693 --> 01:02:38.735
[phone chimes]

835
01:02:49.830 --> 01:02:51.081
[gasping]

836
01:02:51.915 --> 01:02:52.916
[gasps]

837
01:02:55.711 --> 01:02:58.255
[mid-tempo song playing]

838
01:02:58.338 --> 01:02:59.339
Oh! Oh, no!

839
01:03:01.341 --> 01:03:02.342
-Hmm. -Huh?

840
01:03:10.183 --> 01:03:11.977
YOU ARE MY DESTINY

841
01:03:12.060 --> 01:03:13.645
CHRIS K.

842
01:03:18.150 --> 01:03:19.818
[pop song playing]

843
01:04:06.782 --> 01:04:08.784
[Song-yi] What on earth are you up to?

844
01:04:08.867 --> 01:04:10.619
Has he lost his mind?

845
01:04:10.702 --> 01:04:13.538
-If we get eliminated because of you two… -[chuckles]

846
01:04:13.622 --> 01:04:16.792
[Han] Don't worry. I trust your instincts.

847
01:04:17.959 --> 01:04:20.629
You mean this round will be broadcast live on TV?

848
01:04:20.712 --> 01:04:22.047
[Hyeon-ju] Some secret about his birth…

849
01:04:22.130 --> 01:04:24.466
Completely raw and unedited!

850
01:04:24.549 --> 01:04:26.885
[Captain Cook] The challenge for this theme is…

851
01:04:26.968 --> 01:04:29.179
My team doesn't make stupid mistakes.

852
01:04:29.262 --> 01:04:30.514
[Woo-jin] Get out of my sight.

853
01:04:30.597 --> 01:04:31.890
Right now!

854
01:04:31.973 --> 01:04:33.558
This isn't your team, Cha Woo-jin.

855
01:04:33.642 --> 01:04:36.603
-[Woo-jin] You bastard. -[Han] It's our team.
